{"id": "EUVD-2026-86185", "enisaUuid": "05a21cfe-e99c-33b1-a902-c482edc2c4b8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: fix reloc root cleanup in merge_reloc_roots()\n\nIf the root we got has zero root refs in its root item, we are resetting\nthe root's ->reloc_root without using barriers like we do everywhere else.\nSashiko complained about this while reviewing another patch, and it's\ncorrect (see the Link tag below).\n\nAlso, we should not clear BTRFS_ROOT_DEAD_RELOC_TREE from the root unless\nthe root points to the reloc root we have.\n\nFix this by using clear_reloc_root(), which issues the memory barrier\nafter setting the root's ->reloc_root to NULL and before clearing the bit\nBTRFS_ROOT_DEAD_RELOC_TREE from the root.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:32", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29531470b1bf1e8bd2df4941fe913106edbca615", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/415f8665a969d3c906e4fd7c90fcbb4b357886f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee695a968aa73b1e67ccbf2133dc0e54381d32b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0bc25f0a2d1b3e0a691431c4d7aef36afcd527c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab48583aa9948205ff9a6470e23dbff74c565e24", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63d6b1f04cd91c825329712aa526215ffa5d11ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b78fe9563e2d5ae47805f1e5dc722c91fd30e1f8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93798", "GHSA-9c2v-whhq-6g24"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "086c86ea-4f63-3bdb-bd1e-c78d3c7e9eeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7.11 <5.8"}, {"id": "2bb124ae-bcdf-3f95-a934-16f1a1475ea8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1dae7e0e58b484eaa43d530f211098fdeeb0f404 <0bc25f0a2d1b3e0a691431c4d7aef36afcd527c5"}, {"id": "3e